    counselling: "Explain that acute angle-closure is a medical emergency that can cause permanent blindness if untreated. Educate on symptoms to watch for in either eye (pain, blurred vision, haloes around lights, nausea). Explain that the fellow eye is at high risk and should undergo prophylactic laser peripheral iridotomy. Discuss that the condition is related to anatomical predisposition (shallow anterior chamber) and is not caused by anything the patient did wrong. Advise wearing a medical alert bracelet noting glaucoma history.",
